2026-09-24 14:51 Implemented on branch worktree-agent-a4aa130510fb73c94, commit 9e6ecbf (on main 6a75035). New gateway_api probe in OCP::Drift reads the CRD gateways.gateway.networking.k8s.io through Kubernetes::REST (typed IO::K8s CRD, inflates fine with 1.108) and compares the annotation gateway.networking.k8s.io/bundle-version with the pin. It also expects gateway.networking.k8s.io/channel=standard; annotation names checked against the v1.6.1 standard-install.yaml. A missing CRD is drift and carries the remedy (remedy_if_missing). Remedy: new Rex task update_gateway_api, which runs _apply_gateway_api_crds and then _restart_cilium_operator (now shared with install_cilium); params come from remedy_params. ocp update --component gateway_api reaches the same task through the update_<comp> fallback. ocp status prints it generically. Docker make test green 100/1554. Not live-verified. When Cilium and the bundle drift together, both remedies run: an idempotent re-apply plus an extra operator restart.

